IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`

-- Canada Pension Plan Act, Part II, Division E (Payment of Benefits: Amount Payable Under Canada Pension Plan)
-- sections 77 to 80.1. Layer 1: the law, objectively.
--
-- Where a contributor has also contributed to a provincial pension plan (the Quebec Pension Plan is one), only a
-- proportion of each benefit is paid under this Act: section 77 gives the proportion, sections 78 to 79.2 give the
-- amounts it is made of. Section 80 lets an agreement with a province put the whole benefit under one plan.
--
-- Split of the work with piece cp3 (NOTES.md, "Cross-references out of my ranges"): sections 78 to 79.2 say "the total
-- pensionable earnings ... are the amount that their total pensionable earnings would be if the unadjusted pensionable
-- earnings for a year were that proportion of them". The proportion is worked out here, year by year; the recomputation of
-- the total (sections 50 and 51, piece cp3) is taken as a function the caller supplies, and applied here to the scaled amounts.
-- Money is a NUMBER of dollars; a proportion is a NUMBER between 0 and 1. NOTHING means the text does not decide
-- (a proportion whose divisor is nil).

-- out of range: sections 50, 50.1, 50.2 and 51 (piece cp3): the total pensionable earnings of each tier recomputed from each year's unadjusted pensionable earnings, a function supplied by the caller
-- out of range: subparagraphs 53(1)(b)(i) and (ii), 53.1(1)(b)(i) and (ii), 53.2(1)(b)(i) and (ii) (piece cp3): the earnings on which a contribution was made under the Act and under a provincial plan, plain inputs
-- out of range: subsections 55(4) and (5), 55.2(5), (5.1), (5.2), (6), (6.1), (6.2) (piece cp3): the amounts attributed by a division and their totals, plain inputs
-- out of range: section 50 and its tiers (piece cp3): the six totals that section 77 divides, plain inputs

§ `Part II, Division E -- Amount payable under the Canada Pension Plan (sections 77 to 80.1)`

§§ `The figures of one tier for one year`

-- The facts sections 78 to 79.2 read for one year and one tier (base, first additional or second additional).
-- A contributor with no division of unadjusted pensionable earnings in the year leaves the last three fields as they are.
@ref Act s 78, s 79 (src:2426-2429), (src:2441-2444)
DECLARE `cp5 Year of earnings of one tier` HAS
    `unadjusted pensionable earnings of the tier for the year` IS A NUMBER
    `earnings on which a contribution of the tier has been made for the year under this Act` IS A NUMBER
    `earnings on which a contribution of the tier has been made for the year under a provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER
    `the year is a year of a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings` IS A BOOLEAN
    `unadjusted pensionable earnings of the tier attributed by the division` IS A NUMBER
    `total unadjusted pensionable earnings of the tier for the year determined for the division` IS A NUMBER

§§ `Sections 78, 78.1 and 78.2 -- the proportion from contributions made under this Act`

-- The same proportion is stated three times, once for each tier, with different references: a divided by a plus b.
GIVEN a IS A NUMBER
      b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`cp5 helper -- the proportion that a is of the aggregate of a and b` a b MEANS
    IF a PLUS b EQUALS 0 THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST (a DIVIDED BY (a PLUS b))

