§§ `The proportion that applies to a year, and the total pensionable earnings it gives`

-- Sections 78 and 79 (and their additional-tier counterparts) both speak of a year of a division: 78 does not except one,
-- and 79 is written for "a year of a division". A year of a division is read under section 79 and any other year under
-- section 78 (NOTES.md, fork F13).
GIVEN year IS A `cp5 Year of earnings of one tier`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`cp5 helper -- the proportion that applies to a year of one tier` year MEANS
    IF year's `the year is a year of a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings`
    THEN `cp5 helper -- the proportion that earnings attributed are of the total` (year's `unadjusted pensionable earnings of the tier attributed by the division`) (year's `total unadjusted pensionable earnings of the tier for the year determined for the division`)
    ELSE `cp5 helper -- the proportion that a is of the aggregate of a and b` (year's `earnings on which a contribution of the tier has been made for the year under this Act`) (year's `earnings on which a contribution of the tier has been made for the year under a provincial pension plan`)

-- The unadjusted pensionable earnings of the year as the proportion makes them. Nil earnings stay nil whatever the proportion.
GIVEN year IS A `cp5 Year of earnings of one tier`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`cp5 helper -- the unadjusted pensionable earnings of a year as scaled by the proportion` year MEANS
    IF year's `unadjusted pensionable earnings of the tier for the year` EQUALS 0
    THEN JUST 0
    ELSE CONSIDER `cp5 helper -- the proportion that applies to a year of one tier` year
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
         WHEN JUST p THEN JUST (p TIMES (year's `unadjusted pensionable earnings of the tier for the year`))

-- The total pensionable earnings the scaled amounts give: the caller's function stands for sections 50 and 51 (piece cp3).
GIVEN years IS A LIST OF `cp5 Year of earnings of one tier`
      `the total pensionable earnings of the tier that sections 50 and 51 give from the unadjusted pensionable earnings of each year, in the order of the years` IS A FUNCTION FROM LIST OF NUMBER TO NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`cp5 helper -- the total pensionable earnings of a tier attributable to contributions made under this Act` years `the total pensionable earnings of the tier that sections 50 and 51 give from the unadjusted pensionable earnings of each year, in the order of the years` MEANS
    IF any (GIVEN scaled YIELD isNothing scaled) (map (GIVEN year YIELD `cp5 helper -- the unadjusted pensionable earnings of a year as scaled by the proportion` year) years)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (`the total pensionable earnings of the tier that sections 50 and 51 give from the unadjusted pensionable earnings of each year, in the order of the years` (mapMaybe (GIVEN scaled YIELD scaled) (map (GIVEN year YIELD `cp5 helper -- the unadjusted pensionable earnings of a year as scaled by the proportion` year) years)))

@ref Act s 78, s 79 (src:2426-2429), (src:2441-2444)
GIVEN years IS A LIST OF `cp5 Year of earnings of one tier`
      `the total pensionable earnings that section 50 gives from the base unadjusted pensionable earnings of each year, in the order of the years` IS A FUNCTION FROM LIST OF NUMBER TO NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 78 and s 79 — the total pensionable earnings attributable to base contributions made under this Act` years `the total pensionable earnings that section 50 gives from the base unadjusted pensionable earnings of each year, in the order of the years` MEANS
    `cp5 helper -- the total pensionable earnings of a tier attributable to contributions made under this Act` years `the total pensionable earnings that section 50 gives from the base unadjusted pensionable earnings of each year, in the order of the years`

@ref Act s 78.1, s 79.1 (src:2431-2434), (src:2446-2449)
GIVEN years IS A LIST OF `cp5 Year of earnings of one tier`
      `the total first additional pensionable earnings that section 50.1 gives from the first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings of each year, in the order of the years` IS A FUNCTION FROM LIST OF NUMBER TO NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 78.1 and s 79.1 — the total first additional pensionable earnings attributable to first additional contributions made under this Act` years `the total first additional pensionable earnings that section 50.1 gives from the first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings of each year, in the order of the years` MEANS
    `cp5 helper -- the total pensionable earnings of a tier attributable to contributions made under this Act` years `the total first additional pensionable earnings that section 50.1 gives from the first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings of each year, in the order of the years`

@ref Act s 78.2, s 79.2 (src:2436-2439), (src:2451-2454)
GIVEN years IS A LIST OF `cp5 Year of earnings of one tier`
      `the total second additional pensionable earnings that section 50.2 gives from the second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings of each year, in the order of the years` IS A FUNCTION FROM LIST OF NUMBER TO NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 78.2 and s 79.2 — the total second additional pensionable earnings attributable to second additional contributions made under this Act` years `the total second additional pensionable earnings that section 50.2 gives from the second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings of each year, in the order of the years` MEANS
    `cp5 helper -- the total pensionable earnings of a tier attributable to contributions made under this Act` years `the total second additional pensionable earnings that section 50.2 gives from the second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings of each year, in the order of the years`

§§ `Section 77 -- the amount of a benefit payable under this Act`

-- src:2420 | Amount of benefit payable under Act
-- src:2421 | 77 Where, by virtue of any provision of this Act other than this section, a benefit is payable under this Act to or in respect of any contributor, notwithstanding anything in this Part except as provided in section 80, the amount of the benefit that is payable under this Act is an amount equal to that proportion of the amount of the benefit payable to or in respect of the contributor, calculated as provided in this Part without regard to this section, that
-- src:2422 | (a) the aggregate of the contributor’s total pensionable earnings, total first additional pensionable earnings and total second additional pensionable earnings attributable to contributions made under this Act,
-- src:2423 | is to
-- src:2424 | (b) the aggregate of the contributor’s total pensionable earnings, total first additional pensionable earnings and total second additional pensionable earnings.
@ref Act s 77 (src:2421-2424)
GIVEN `the total pensionable earnings attributable to base contributions made under this Act` IS A NUMBER
      `the total first additional pensionable earnings attributable to first additional contributions made under this Act` IS A NUMBER
      `the total second additional pensionable earnings attributable to second additional contributions made under this Act` IS A NUMBER
      `the total pensionable earnings` IS A NUMBER
      `the total first additional pensionable earnings` IS A NUMBER
      `the total second additional pensionable earnings` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 77 — the proportion of a benefit that is payable under this Act` `the total pensionable earnings attributable to base contributions made under this Act` `the total first additional pensionable earnings attributable to first additional contributions made under this Act` `the total second additional pensionable earnings attributable to second additional contributions made under this Act` `the total pensionable earnings` `the total first additional pensionable earnings` `the total second additional pensionable earnings` MEANS
    IF (`the total pensionable earnings` PLUS `the total first additional pensionable earnings` PLUS `the total second additional pensionable earnings`) EQUALS 0
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST ((`the total pensionable earnings attributable to base contributions made under this Act` PLUS `the total first additional pensionable earnings attributable to first additional contributions made under this Act` PLUS `the total second additional pensionable earnings attributable to second additional contributions made under this Act`) DIVIDED BY (`the total pensionable earnings` PLUS `the total first additional pensionable earnings` PLUS `the total second additional pensionable earnings`))

§§ `Section 80 -- agreements with provinces`

-- Subsection 80(1)(e) and subsection 80(2): where an agreement puts the whole benefit under one plan, the whole amount is
-- deemed payable under that plan "notwithstanding section 77". The Minister's power to make the agreement (the chapeau,
-- (a) to (d), and subsection (3) on financial adjustments) is machinery: NOTES.md, coverage table.
-- src:2455 | Agreements with provinces
-- src:2456 | 80 (1) Notwithstanding section 77, the Minister, with the approval of the Governor in Council, may on behalf of the Government of Canada enter into an agreement with the appropriate authority of a province providing a comprehensive pension plan to provide for the administration and coordination of this Act and the provincial pension plan in respect of persons who are contributors under this Act or the provincial plan or both, including, without limiting the generality of the foregoing,
-- src:2457 | (a) the determination and payment of any benefit, or portion thereof, payable under this Act or under the provincial pension plan;
-- src:2458 | (b) the determination, processing and approval of divisions of unadjusted pensionable earnings under this Act and under the provincial pension plan;
-- src:2459 | (c) the determination, processing and approval of applications for assignments, under this Act or under the provincial pension plan, of a retirement pension to the spouse or common-law partner of a contributor;
-- src:2460 | (d) the exchange of such information obtained under this Act or under the provincial pension plan as is necessary to give effect to the agreement; and
-- src:2461 | (e) the payment under this Act in accordance with the agreement of the whole amount of any benefit payable to or in respect of a contributor, calculated as provided in this Part without regard to section 77, in which case the whole amount of that benefit shall be deemed to be payable under this Act to or in respect of that contributor.
-- src:2462 | Saving
-- src:2463 | (2) Where, in accordance with any agreement entered into under subsection (1), the whole amount of any benefit payable to or in respect of a contributor, calculated in a manner similar to that described in paragraph (1)(e), is payable under the provincial pension plan referred to in that subsection, the whole amount of that benefit shall be deemed to be payable under the provincial pension plan to or in respect of that contributor.
-- src:2464 | Provision for making of financial adjustments
-- src:2465 | (3) Any agreement entered into under subsection (1) may provide for the making of any financial adjustments required to be made by reason of any payments made to or in respect of a contributor in accordance with that agreement, and for the crediting or charging of the amount of those adjustments to the Canada Pension Plan Account or the Additional Canada Pension Plan Account, as the case may be.
@ref Act s 80(1)(e), s 80(2) (src:2461), (src:2463)
DECLARE `cp5 Where an agreement under section 80 puts the whole of a benefit` IS ONE OF
    `no agreement under section 80 puts the whole of the benefit under one plan`
    `an agreement under section 80 puts the whole of the benefit under this Act`
    `an agreement under section 80 puts the whole of the benefit under the provincial pension plan`

@ref Act s 77, s 80(1)(e), s 80(2) (src:2421), (src:2461), (src:2463)
GIVEN `the amount of the benefit calculated as provided in this Part without regard to section 77` IS A NUMBER
      `the proportion of the benefit payable under this Act under section 77` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      agreement IS A `cp5 Where an agreement under section 80 puts the whole of a benefit`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 77 and s 80 — the amount of the benefit that is payable under this Act` `the amount of the benefit calculated as provided in this Part without regard to section 77` `the proportion of the benefit payable under this Act under section 77` agreement MEANS
    CONSIDER agreement
    WHEN `an agreement under section 80 puts the whole of the benefit under this Act` THEN JUST `the amount of the benefit calculated as provided in this Part without regard to section 77`
    WHEN `an agreement under section 80 puts the whole of the benefit under the provincial pension plan` THEN JUST 0
    WHEN `no agreement under section 80 puts the whole of the benefit under one plan` THEN
        CONSIDER `the proportion of the benefit payable under this Act under section 77`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST p THEN JUST (p TIMES `the amount of the benefit calculated as provided in this Part without regard to section 77`)

§§ `Section 80.1 -- agreements respecting the apportionment of payments`

-- Subsections 80.1(1) and (2) (the power to make the agreement and the rules it provides) are machinery. Subsection (3) says
-- what an agreement does for a beneficiary; subsection (4) says what no agreement may do.
-- src:2476 | Limitation
-- src:2477 | (4) An agreement may not
-- src:2478 | (a) change a person’s eligibility to receive a benefit as a disabled contributor’s child or the amount of that benefit;
-- src:2479 | (b) change the determination of months that are excluded from a beneficiary’s contributory period by reason of disability;
-- src:2480 | (c) result in a beneficiary receiving, in respect of any month, disability benefits under this Act and payments under the other law or activity that are less than the disability benefits that would be otherwise payable under this Act for the month if there were no such agreement; or
-- src:2481 | (d) result in a beneficiary receiving, in respect of any month, disability benefits under this Act that are greater than the disability benefits that would otherwise be payable under this Act if there were no agreement.
@ref Act s 80.1(4) (src:2477-2481)
GIVEN `the agreement changes a person's eligibility to receive a benefit as a disabled contributor's child or the amount of that benefit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agreement changes the determination of months that are excluded from a beneficiary's contributory period by reason of disability` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disability benefits under this Act that the agreement makes payable for the month` IS A NUMBER
      `the payments under the other law or activity for the month` IS A NUMBER
      `the disability benefits that would otherwise be payable under this Act for the month if there were no agreement` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 80.1(4) — the agreement is within the limits that subsection (4) sets` `the agreement changes a person's eligibility to receive a benefit as a disabled contributor's child or the amount of that benefit` `the agreement changes the determination of months that are excluded from a beneficiary's contributory period by reason of disability` `the disability benefits under this Act that the agreement makes payable for the month` `the payments under the other law or activity for the month` `the disability benefits that would otherwise be payable under this Act for the month if there were no agreement` MEANS
    -- (a) change a person's eligibility to receive, or the amount of, a disabled contributor's child's benefit
        (NOT `the agreement changes a person's eligibility to receive a benefit as a disabled contributor's child or the amount of that benefit`)
    -- (b) change the determination of months excluded from a beneficiary's contributory period by reason of disability
    AND (NOT `the agreement changes the determination of months that are excluded from a beneficiary's contributory period by reason of disability`)
    -- (c) result in the disability benefits under this Act and the payments under the other law or activity totalling
    --     less than the disability benefits otherwise payable under this Act
    AND (`the disability benefits under this Act that the agreement makes payable for the month` PLUS `the payments under the other law or activity for the month`) AT LEAST `the disability benefits that would otherwise be payable under this Act for the month if there were no agreement`
    -- (d) result in disability benefits under this Act greater than those otherwise payable
    AND `the disability benefits under this Act that the agreement makes payable for the month` AT MOST `the disability benefits that would otherwise be payable under this Act for the month if there were no agreement`

-- src:2474 | Effect of agreement
-- src:2475 | (3) Notwithstanding anything in this Act, but subject to subsection (4), where an agreement entered into pursuant to subsection (1) applies in respect of a beneficiary, the only amounts that may be payable as disability benefits to the beneficiary under this Act are the amounts provided for by the agreement.
@ref Act s 80.1(3) (src:2475)
GIVEN `an agreement under subsection 80.1(1) applies in respect of the beneficiary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agreement is within the limits that subsection (4) sets` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount the agreement provides as the disability benefit payable under this Act for the month` IS A NUMBER
      `the disability benefit otherwise payable under this Act for the month` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 80.1(3) — the disability benefit payable under this Act for the month` `an agreement under subsection 80.1(1) applies in respect of the beneficiary` `the agreement is within the limits that subsection (4) sets` `the amount the agreement provides as the disability benefit payable under this Act for the month` `the disability benefit otherwise payable under this Act for the month` MEANS
    IF NOT `an agreement under subsection 80.1(1) applies in respect of the beneficiary`
    THEN JUST `the disability benefit otherwise payable under this Act for the month`
    -- (NOTES.md, fork F25) "the only amounts that may be payable as disability benefits ... are the amounts provided for by the agreement",
    -- "subject to subsection (4)": an agreement outside the limits is one the text does not allow, and does not say what then is payable
    ELSE IF `the agreement is within the limits that subsection (4) sets`
         THEN JUST `the amount the agreement provides as the disability benefit payable under this Act for the month`
         ELSE NOTHING
